infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Re-aggregate on read vs stored aggregate
  desc Same workspace-revenue number — pay the cost on every read, or once per write
  compares
    - label Normalized: SUM on every dashboard load
      children
        - label No duplicate fact to reconcile
          desc Revenue is always derived live from order_items — never stale
        - label Correct under ~1M order_items
          desc Below ~1M rows the live SUM JOIN is cheap enough to ignore
        - label Bottleneck above ~10M rows
          desc Every dashboard request re-aggregates the full order history
    - label Denormalized: stored aggregate column
      children
        - label Dashboard reads one column per workspace
          desc workspace_revenue_cents replaces a SUM over millions of rows
        - label ~1-5 µs write overhead
          desc One BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE trigger per order_items write
        - label Must be reconciled by something
          desc The trigger keeps the duplicate consistent at write time
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
